{
  "_readme": "GAME CONTENT, DRAFT PENDING PRODUCER REVIEW (every name, line and title). The NPC dialogue layer (docs/design/area-zero.md and docs/design/grove.md \"NPCs\" (D2) \u2014 the two share this one file, per grove.md's reconciliation note): Npcs (NpcId, DisplayName, PortraitKey = an art-manifest key, '' = a placeholder portrait), Lines (LineId, NpcId, Conditions, Text, Priority; a scene's own lines carry scene:{SceneId} so the Grove's resolution never picks them; a Grove condition is kind:params, see Tutorial.NpcConditionKinds, built live from account state by Npc.NpcRules.BuildFacts) and Scenes (SceneId, Title, LineIds: an ordered run of lines a story location plays, regions.json FixedNodes SceneId). D2 adds: Requests (RequestId, NpcId, Conditions, ItemId, Count, RewardKind, RewardId, Text \u2014 a one-off ask for a Grove item, Grove.GroveItemInventory, fulfilled once via Npc.NpcRules.FulfillRequest) and SideStories (StoryId, NpcId, DisplayName, Chapters: ChapterId, Conditions, Text, RequestItemId, RequestCount, RewardKind, RewardId, LoreId, NextChapterId \u2014 an optional per-NPC chapter chain, never required for the main campaign, tracked in PlayerSave.Npc.SideStories) and Lore (LoreId, Title, Text \u2014 the dialogue layer's own small codex, a request's or a chapter's reward, separate from Grove's and discovery's). v1 cast: the Grove Keeper (Hearthglen's mentor, who now also tends the Grove hub), the Trader, the Wandering Scholar and Forest Folk. No combat power anywhere, no gold that buys power; a title is earned only through an achievement (AchievementKinds.SideStoryComplete), never a request or side-story reward directly \u2014 RewardKind decor/look is mechanically wired (CheckReward) but v1 content authors only lore and none, the same 'wire it, do not author it yet' stance grove-library.json took for look rewards. Validated by BeastCraft.Tutorial.DialogueValidator (content load and the EditMode tests). Tone: content-bible.md (warm, wonder first; nobody dies).",
